From: David Edmundson <davidedmundson@kde.org>
Date: Sun, 25 May 2025 19:15:06 +0000
Subject: wayland: Avoid using expose events to commit parents on subsurfaces moves

When a subsurface moves the update is double buffered with that parent
window committing a change.

We need to force a redraw on the offchance that the application is not
also rendering a frame, but we do not need to force that to happen
early, it's best if it's in line with the normal frame callback cycle.
As such the expose event is not the right tool for the job,
requestUpdate is better.

This massively improves performance when a window has mulitple
subsurfaces.

Change-Id: If6eb3b12053eab49a4b9077c289bfcc74f331863
Reviewed-by: David Redondo <qt@david-redondo.de>
Origin: upstream, https://code.qt.io/cgit/qt/qtbase.git/commit/?id=d6d2a75cdbfe2a97ef211af09b71dd1a6bd00392
Applied-Upstream: dev (committed 2026-07-09, Qt 6.13), not in 6.11.3 or 6.12.1
Comment: Carried for queue row 863: a stereo window of its own moved during the backing store's flush made the parent
 repaint synchronously from inside that flush, which freed the texture list the flush was reading. The hunk of
 qwaylandwindow_p.h is adapted to 6.11.2 (its context differs); the change is upstream's.
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
---
diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylandwindow.cpp b/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylandwindow.cpp
index f5c0bf7e..7c5d93bc 100644
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylandwindow.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylandwindow.cpp
@@ -483,10 +483,8 @@ void QWaylandWindow::setGeometry_helper(const QRect &rect)
         mSubSurfaceWindow->set_position(rect.x() + m.left(), rect.y() + m.top());
 
         QWaylandWindow *parentWindow = mSubSurfaceWindow->parent();
-        if (parentWindow && parentWindow->isExposed()) {
-            QRect parentExposeGeometry(QPoint(), parentWindow->geometry().size());
-            parentWindow->sendExposeEvent(parentExposeGeometry);
-        }
+        if (parentWindow)
+            parentWindow->requestForcedUpdate();
     }
 }
 
@@ -1231,7 +1229,7 @@ bool QWaylandWindow::createDecoration()
         // size and are not redrawn, leaving the new buffer empty. As a simple
         // work-around, we trigger a full extra update whenever the client-side
         // window decorations are toggled while the window is showing.
-        window()->requestUpdate();
+        requestForcedUpdate();
     }
 
     return mWindowDecoration.get();
@@ -1860,10 +1858,23 @@ void QWaylandWindow::handleUpdate()
     }
 }
 
+void QWaylandWindow::requestForcedUpdate()
+{
+    mPendingForcedUpdate = true;
+    window()->requestUpdate();
+}
+
 void QWaylandWindow::deliverUpdateRequest()
 {
     qCDebug(lcWaylandBackingstore) << "deliverUpdateRequest";
     QPlatformWindow::deliverUpdateRequest();
+
+    // an update request doesn't always force a commit if the window isn't damaged, so also force it
+    if (mPendingForcedUpdate) {
+        mPendingForcedUpdate = false;
+        QRect exposeGeometry(QPoint(), geometry().size());
+        QWindowSystemInterface::handleExposeEvent<QWindowSystemInterface::SynchronousDelivery>(window(), exposeGeometry);
+    }
 }
 
 void QWaylandWindow::addAttachOffset(const QPoint point)
diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylandwindow_p.h b/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylandwindow_p.h
index 259f1673..d159d1b1 100644
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylandwindow_p.h
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylandwindow_p.h
@@ -232,6 +232,7 @@ public:
     void timerEvent(QTimerEvent *event) override;
     void requestUpdate() override;
     void handleUpdate();
+    void requestForcedUpdate();
     void deliverUpdateRequest() override;
 
     void setXdgActivationToken(const QString &token);
@@ -317,6 +318,7 @@ protected:
     std::atomic_bool mFrameCallbackTimedOut = false; // Whether the frame callback has timed out
     int mFrameCallbackCheckIntervalTimerId = -1;
     QAtomicInt mWaitingForUpdateDelivery = false;
+    bool mPendingForcedUpdate = false; // The window should force a redraw at the next fame callback
 
     bool mWaitingForFrameCallback = false; // Protected by mFrameSyncMutex
     QElapsedTimer mFrameCallbackElapsedTimer; // Protected by mFrameSyncMutex
